      "MeasuredUseReceipt": "Versioned signed fact with unique useId, grantId for trial uses, proposalHash/knowledgeId/contentHash, baseline/candidate (or post-promotion observed-use) role, pairId when comparing, source/profile/build/model/config/task/goal/policy bindings, actual sessionId/callId/Session event sequence/hash, exact rendered tool result hash, actual provider request hash, final output artifact manifest, independently executed oracle/checker identity/results, actual error/retry/tool/cost observations, measurement definition and immutable content-addressed evidence references. Candidate use requires a real matching injection; baseline must explicitly attest absence of candidate exposure. Unknown/failure/zero opportunities are explicit and never pass.",
      "MeasuredTrialReceipt": "Versioned signed aggregate referencing proposal, grant, measurement definition and every preregistered use receipt including failures/unknowns. Carries raw baseline/candidate Count numerator/denominator values with real opportunities; runtime recomputes rates/lift rather than trusting a claimed score. Completeness/order/exclusions/model-task equality and safety observations are checked.",
      "CandidateTrialProjection": "Reuse existing public CandidateTrial summary shape if sufficient: trialHash references authenticated measured-trial receipt, counters are projections only. It must never be read as authority. A summary alone cannot enable apply/recovery.",
      "DurableProjectJournal": "Add explicitly versioned local trial-authorized, use-measured and trial-measured records to the existing knowledge journal owner (not core SessionEventMap). These must be real defined payloads with receipt hashes and independent authority references. Define a new local journal version if the existing closed event schema is extended; old bytes stay retained. Old semantic checks/UI success/legacy trial summaries remain uncredited. Historical model read authority may be preserved only by explicit authenticated migration of its existing facts, never by assigning new trial success. Existing Session knowledge/retrieved and knowledge/injected already capture model-visible rendered content and remain structurally unchanged."
    },
    "authoritySeparation": {
      "evaluator": "Externally provisioned public trust anchor only in ARK. Private evaluator signing authority must be outside candidate-author/launcher access; owner controls oracle and signing policy. Same UID with readable private file does not establish independence. A different model is neither necessary nor sufficient.",
      "journal": "Separate product-owned local signing authority for crash consistency. Keep sealPromotion/validatePromotion for that role only; expose distinct evaluator authority ID and journal signer ID. Domain-separate signature payload kinds/versions; reject same-key-role configuration and wrong-role replay.",
      "facade": "Extend current injected facade only for measured trial/use requests and public validation of their evidence. verifyCandidate/validateCandidateResult stay evaluator checks; sealPromotion/validatePromotion stay local. Do not make an existing local seal certify independent evaluation.",
      "replay": "readKnowledgeEventLog must revalidate the referenced external candidate/proposal/grant/trial/use chain before any positive trust/utility/canonical record is folded; local verified/promoted event seals alone remain insufficient. This must run at model admission, import, apply and WAL recovery, with a trusted artifact resolver rather than caller-chosen paths.",
      "provisioning": "Use a versioned launcher-owned descriptor containing evaluator public trust and fixed validated endpoint/executable/build digest/artifact-root locator, plus separate journal key handle and policy. Native ShellContract must receive only this explicitly selected protected descriptor through product-owned launch configuration, retaining its environment allowlist. Do not inherit all ARK_* env or load a project-controlled executable/key. Missing owner/descriptor remains unavailable."
